<?xml version="1.0"?>
<keys name="Linea default">

<!--
This file contains the default Linea keyboard shortcuts.

========== Actions ==========

- The "keys" attribute contains a comma separated list of shortcuts using
  tokens: Cmd, Ctrl, Shift, Alt.
  "Cmd" is a generic platform-sepcific command key.
  On macOS, Cmd maps to real Command key; on other platforms, Cmd maps to Control key.
  On macOS, Alt maps to Option key; on other platforms, Alt maps to Alt key.
  Ctrl is always Control key and Shift is always Shift key.
  The first entry will be listed in menus.

- The "action" attribute contains the full action name.

- NOTE: Cmd+Ctrl+key only makes sense on macOS, elsewhere it is a Ctrl+key.

- NOTE 2: Alternative key sequences are separated by semicolon+space (; )
  A colon (,) in a sequence means that the keys need to be pressed in succession (multi-key shortcuts).

=========== Notes ===========

This file is the default keymap for LineaDraw. User customizations are stored separately.

-->

